course: dictionary
lesson: 15642
title: Land, Earth and Sky
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Terrestrial means to do with land, or with the planet Earth. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are the context and they leave clues. «Lions and ants are terrestrial animals.» Lions and ants live on land, so terrestrial must mean living on land.
explain: «Fish are aquatic, but lions are terrestrial.» Aquatic means living in water, and the word but shows that terrestrial is different from it. Swap your meaning into the sentence: living on land makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Terrestrial can also be about space. «Mars and Earth are terrestrial planets, made of rock.» Terrestrial planets are the rocky planets. «Creatures from beyond Earth are extra-terrestrial.» The extra- at the start is your clue that it means from outside Earth.
explain: On TV, the word has a special meaning. «Our terrestrial channels come from transmitters on the ground, not from a satellite.» The words on the ground and not from a satellite tell you that terrestrial TV is sent from the ground.
fact: Terrestrial means living on land or growing on land, not in water or the air.
fact: Terrestrial also means to do with the planet Earth, not space.
fact: «Terrestrial animals», such as lions and ants, live on land.
fact: «Terrestrial planets», such as Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars, are rocky.
fact: «Extra-terrestrial» means from beyond Earth, like an alien (an ET).
exercise: «Lions and ants are terrestrial animals.» What does terrestrial mean here? | Living in the air | Living in space | *Living on land | Living in water
exercise: «Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars are terrestrial planets.» What does terrestrial tell you about these planets? | They are covered in water | They are made of gas | *They are rocky | They are very hot stars
exercise: «Fish are aquatic, but lions are terrestrial.» Which word means living in water? | animals | *aquatic | lions | terrestrial
test: «Our terrestrial TV channels are sent from transmitters on the ground.» What does terrestrial TV mean? | Sent through a satellite in space | Only shown at night | Shown only in cinemas | *Sent from transmitters on the ground
test: «The aliens in the film were extra-terrestrial.» What does extra-terrestrial mean? | Living under the sea | Made of paper | Living in the same town | *From beyond Earth
exam: Which word is the opposite of terrestrial when we talk about animals? | *Aquatic | Planet | Sky | Rocky
